cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use llmaudit in research or an evaluation report, please cite the software and include the version or commit you used."
title: "LLM Evaluation with Human Audits"
type: software
version: "0.2.0.dev0"
authors:
  - family-names: Leng
    given-names: Yan
repository-code: "https://github.com/yleng/llm-measurement-audit-release"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Human-audited inference for LLM-as-a-judge evaluations. Combines automated
  scores with probability-sampled human ratings to estimate treatment effects
  in randomized experiments and paired model differences on shared prompts,
  with confidence intervals and explicit sampling requirements.
keywords:
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - LLM evaluation
  - human evaluation
  - measurement error
  - randomized experiments
  - paired model comparison
  - prediction-powered inference
  - augmented inverse-probability weighting
